Performance: a `[NinoType]` struct that holds a reference (a string, a collection) and no class or custom formatter, nullable or not, is written 1.7 to 2.6 times as fast and read 1.2 to 1.9 times as fast, alone and in arrays: its body now works on a local reader and writer and is inlined where it is small. On GitHub runners, 100 `ManagedStruct?` are written in 437 ns instead of 1,056 on EPYC 7763, 287 instead of 644 on EPYC 9V74 and 309 instead of 762 on Neoverse-N2, and read in 1,202 ns instead of 1,615, 909 instead of 1,240 and 1,428 instead of 1,824.
